KPL/MYB

TDB - TT at the geocentre: Fairhead & Bretagnon series
=======================================================

   S(t) = sum over terms of  A * t^k * sin(w * t + phi)          [seconds]

   t    time since J2000.0 in units of MYB_SERIES_TDB_TT_UNIT seconds (Julian
        millennia: 365250 days of 86400 s), measured on the TDB scale itself.
   Each term is four numbers: k (power of t), A (s), w (rad per unit), phi (rad).

Sources
   L. Fairhead, P. Bretagnon, "An analytical formula for the time transformation
   TB-TT", Astron. Astrophys. 229, 240-247 (1990), in its full form: terms 1-787,
   as supplied by Fairhead to P. T. Wallace (1990) and distributed with IAU SOFA
   (iau_DTDB); per the SOFA notes the adaptation differs from the original at the
   1e-20 s level.
   The last five terms are the adjustments to the JPL planetary masses of
   SOFA/ERFA iauDtdb/eraDtdb ("Adjustments to use JPL planetary masses instead of
   IAU"); the t^2 term is written as sin(0*t + pi/2) = 1.
   Numbers copied verbatim from ERFA src/dtdb.c (BSD-3-Clause, derived from SOFA),
   revision 1a8044cde5b7763295d472a6443387239127c6c8.

Accuracy (ERFA eraDtdb note 7): better than +/- 3 ns over 1950-2050 relative to time
ephemerides integrated with JPL DE405. The series is a model of the relativistic
TCB-TCG relation; numerical integration of an ephemeris is the definitive method
(planned module rel). Only the geocentric part is given here: the topocentric terms
depend on the observer and belong to the observer's proper time.

